WEBVTT

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:13.950
There's no way out?

00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:18.750
That's right! It's not just us, the ship is trapped, too!

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:21.650
So that was their plan.

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:23.820
What do we do?

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:27.720
I wish I could say we could manage if we stopped the spread of the fire...

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:30.420
But it's probably hopeless...

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:38.280
That boy will come!

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:41.420
Garrod Ran will definitely come!

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:46.820
Damn it!

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.120
You're right! I forgot to get a picture!

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:52.280
That's not what I meant!

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:57.650
You will come, Garrod.

00:00:57.850 --> 00:00:59.980
Our sense of style demands it.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:06.120
I have no choice but to go?

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:27.180
I have to go!

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:36.920
<b>After War</b>

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:36.920
<b>GUNDAM</b>

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:44.430
<b>The dream I'd nearly forgotten is beginning to stir,</b>

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:47.390
<b>little by little</b>

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:51.940
<b>filling in the gaps in my heart</b>

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:59.320
<b>The instant my frozen memories begin to awaken,</b>

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:08.830
<b>my only wish is for the future that is about to begin</b>

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:12.380
<b>I'll reach out with both hands</b>

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:16.400
<b>and embrace that dream I once had</b>

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:20.010
<b>I want to go on believing</b>

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:23.940
<b>without ever letting go or giving up</b>

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:27.580
<b>Until the day comes when I grab hold...</b>

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:31.440
<b>...of that dream I once had,</b>

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.980
<b>I want to keep chasing after it</b>

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:40.860
<b>without ever forgetting my hopes and dreams</b>

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:51.420
<b>Episode 9</b>

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:51.420
<b>"As it Rains in the Streets..."</b>

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:58.850
So what do you want to do? Go down fighting with the Freeden?

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:03.520
That ship's carrying my precious treasure!

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:05.120
If you want to run, feel free.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:09.450
I can't do that. I'm on the clock, you see.

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:11.320
What the...? What the...?

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:15.180
I know that attack!

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:16.950
I have a bad feeling about this...

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:25.450
Roabea!

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:38.320
How I've longed for this day to come.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:47.120
It's finally time to get our revenge, Brother.

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:48.850
If that's how you want it!

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:00.520
Party crashers?

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:05.080
Perfect timing. I'll use the distraction to go after the ship.

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:28.150
Garrod!

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:29.750
This is all your fault-

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:36.280
I...

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:44.420
Tiffa, you're in there, right? I...

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:45.720
No.

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:48.080
I don't want to see anyone right now.

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:55.680
You have nowhere to go back to, right?

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:15.750
Oh, dear. Telling them he couldn't be moved was a waste of breath.

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:43.580
You're mine!

00:05:52.980 --> 00:05:53.780
What?

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:57.420
That's-

00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:58.580
Well, I'll be!

00:06:01.180 --> 00:06:02.950
Ta-dah!

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:06.720
The invincible mobile suit pilot Garrod Ran has arrived...

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:09.520
...in the Gundam X to save you all!

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:11.680
Garrod?!

00:06:11.780 --> 00:06:14.180
Where's he been all this time?!

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:16.980
Waiting for the right time to come back!

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:23.420
Garrod...

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:25.820
You're still not ready...

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:27.850
Let's do this!

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:39.620
Move the ship!

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:41.580
Move it? Move it where?!

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:43.750
There's nothing but fire in all directions!

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:47.680
Look. There's a lake beyond the forest at  3 o'clock.

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:52.820
Oh, right! A lake! That's our acting captain!

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:56.380
I'm impressed, you finding us a way out just in case!

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:07.920
The Freeden's on the move! Let's meet up with them!

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:09.520
Roger that!

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:20.180
You think you can escape?

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:27.650
These two are also Gundams! Capture them!

00:07:28.250 --> 00:07:29.320
Don't even try!

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:52.350
I'm surprised you came back, runaway. I heard all about it.

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:55.780
I'm surprised you came back like it was nothing!

00:07:55.880 --> 00:07:59.520
Yeah, I'm the type who doesn't dwell on things!

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:01.250
Hey, you two!

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:04.750
There's no telling when those guys will attack.

00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:07.220
Don't let your guard down until we reach that lake.

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:09.580
Yeah, fine...

00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:23.620
You're awake, I see.

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:25.280
Where am I?

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:28.550
Not in Heaven, at any rate.

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:31.820
What do you mean, stop the ship?

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:36.750
I... just have a feeling. But you should-

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:39.220
That's not a good enough reason!

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:43.220
But she has special powers, doesn't she?

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:45.180
I think the Captain would listen to her.

00:08:45.650 --> 00:08:46.780
I'm not-

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:52.420
Rejoice, everyone. My patient is awake at last.

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:55.220
Captain!

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:57.250
How are your injuries?

00:08:57.350 --> 00:08:59.080
Are you feeling better?

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:02.150
I'm sorry I worried you all.

00:09:02.420 --> 00:09:04.820
I hate to get right down to business, but tell me what I've missed.

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:20.120
Keep wasting your time over there.

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:32.720
Then you want us to follow her advice, sir?

00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:35.980
I do. Turn around, and quickly.

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:39.850
Her advice means more than a decision based on battlefield conditions?

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:43.280
I would make the same decision even without Tiffa's advice.

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:46.980
What's that?!

00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:57.350
Someone's standing on the water!

00:09:58.220 --> 00:10:00.020
What now, a wizard?

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:06.520
What's that?!

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:26.980
Welcome to the Lake of Fire, gentlemen.

00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:31.020
Son of a... They were waiting here for us?!

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:40.950
They're duds!

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:43.680
They probably got wet from being in the water.

00:10:48.150 --> 00:10:49.180
Look, it's-

00:10:54.950 --> 00:10:55.780
What?!

00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:58.020
Commence bombardment!

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:15.420
Crap, this is what he meant by "Lake of Fire"?

00:11:18.050 --> 00:11:20.720
Hull temperature climbing rapidly!

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:23.120
Fires have broken out in Engine Room 1!

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:24.680
Sara!

00:11:25.180 --> 00:11:27.620
Don't worry. You're doing fine.

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:30.280
Captain...

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:40.450
Sara?

00:11:59.850 --> 00:12:01.750
We wasted time on them.

00:12:01.850 --> 00:12:05.080
Plus, I used up all of my Megasonic Cannon's energy.

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:07.820
Don't worry, you have me for backup.

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:12.280
So let's go, Brother. Let's go join them!

00:12:17.850 --> 00:12:18.650
Garrod!

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:23.250
I'm gonna destroy them! I'm not gonna stand there and let them sink us!

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:26.620
What the...?

00:12:28.820 --> 00:12:30.880
We meet again, boy.

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:33.580
I know that voice! Ennil El!

00:12:34.050 --> 00:12:35.120
Son of a...

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:39.220
I thought I said that you won't escape.

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:41.350
I suggest you say your prayers.

00:12:48.850 --> 00:12:50.780
Hey! Are you okay? Hang in there!

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:53.220
What is it?

00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:57.750
Two of my mechanics got hurt in that attack! Come right away!

00:12:58.280 --> 00:12:59.550
Understood.

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:25.680
If you do as I say, I'll spare your crewmates.

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:26.980
Come again?

00:13:27.020 --> 00:13:29.250
I like you, boy.

00:13:31.050 --> 00:13:33.150
You should be more honest with yourself.

00:13:34.220 --> 00:13:37.620
I can tell. You felt ashamed after what we did.

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:42.950
That's not true!

00:13:43.450 --> 00:13:46.420
That woman and Garrod, they...?

00:13:48.780 --> 00:13:50.580
We didn't do anything!

00:13:56.880 --> 00:13:58.850
The way you put up a brave facade is adorable.

00:13:58.950 --> 00:14:00.450
Why, you...!

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:06.980
It's not too late. I can make your loneliness go away.

00:14:33.250 --> 00:14:35.220
T-Tiffa...

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:41.150
My home... My place to return to...

00:14:42.680 --> 00:14:44.780
...is this ship!

00:14:55.850 --> 00:14:59.750
Garrod, you're the only one who can get us out of this!

00:15:01.680 --> 00:15:05.220
What? There's no other way?

00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:12.150
Bridge! On my signal, get us underway, emergency speed!

00:15:21.850 --> 00:15:23.280
Change in plans, huh?

00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:26.420
I guess we have to put our faith in him.

00:15:27.850 --> 00:15:29.480
Freeden! Emergency liftoff!

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:44.050
They're ready to meet their fate, huh? Charge them! Hunt them down!

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:59.880
Fools, do you think you can win against my ship here on the Lake of Fire?

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:07.520
Much more of this, and it'll cause the engines to explode!

00:16:07.620 --> 00:16:08.720
Sara!

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:17.620
We'll be all right.

00:16:21.520 --> 00:16:24.520
Why did they run?

00:16:25.280 --> 00:16:26.180
What's that?

00:16:26.280 --> 00:16:28.750
I know what you mean. Wait, look there!

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:38.020
This battle has been decided. We'll try again another time.

00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:39.820
Why?!

00:16:42.380 --> 00:16:44.380
Very well, Brother...

00:16:51.580 --> 00:16:55.980
There's a 4.03 second gap between laser lock and microwave arrival.

00:16:56.720 --> 00:16:58.120
Can I make it?

00:17:03.350 --> 00:17:05.720
Captain! We can't take any more!

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:10.780
We're counting on you, Garrod!

00:17:16.520 --> 00:17:17.850
There it is!

00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:28.050
Now!

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:31.480
Four! Three!

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:33.380
Two! One!

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:37.380
Come on down!

00:18:25.880 --> 00:18:28.550
Clever, triggering a steam explosion by having...

00:18:28.650 --> 00:18:31.450
...the microwave beam strike the lake directly...

00:18:32.320 --> 00:18:34.880
...and now this miraculous rain.

00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:36.550
You've got style.

00:18:44.820 --> 00:18:47.880
They're all wet. Let's get those bandages changed.

00:18:49.920 --> 00:18:51.350
Sorry.

00:18:58.350 --> 00:19:03.550
"As it rains in the streets, so too do tears fall in my heart."

00:19:03.850 --> 00:19:05.680
Rimbaud, I think?

00:19:05.780 --> 00:19:07.980
No, it's by Verlaine.

00:19:19.120 --> 00:19:23.520
Basically, we want you on the payroll until his wounds are fully healed.

00:19:24.320 --> 00:19:27.180
Be exclusive to the Freeden, huh?

00:19:27.780 --> 00:19:31.080
I don't think I'll be finding a hiding spot for my treasure anytime soon.

00:19:31.180 --> 00:19:33.050
May as well crash here a while.

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:35.050
I think that's for the best, too!

00:19:35.120 --> 00:19:36.680
Stay out of this, lady!

00:19:37.350 --> 00:19:40.050
I was getting tired of the drifter lifestyle, anyway.

00:19:43.750 --> 00:19:45.450
Also, Garrod...

00:19:46.820 --> 00:19:50.120
As long as you're with us, no further unauthorized actions will be tolerated.

00:19:50.650 --> 00:19:52.820
As your punishment, you're to look after Tiffa.

00:19:54.580 --> 00:19:56.120
Who, me?!

00:19:56.220 --> 00:19:58.050
You played us, you bum!

00:19:58.150 --> 00:20:01.420
You sly dog you! Don't do anything I wouldn't do!

00:20:01.520 --> 00:20:05.120
Cut it out! We're not like that! I just-

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:06.280
Oh! Hi, Tiffa!

00:20:12.650 --> 00:20:14.180
Tiffa?

00:20:15.250 --> 00:20:19.080
This is the place we need to go to.

00:20:20.550 --> 00:20:23.550
You're saying that we will find a Newtype there?

00:20:33.320 --> 00:20:37.680
Does this mean that we now have archenemies, Brother?

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:43.280
If we don't view them as such, it will hinder the completion of our mission.

00:20:44.050 --> 00:20:45.420
One thing, Olba...

00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:49.450
I think your line earlier about our "sense of style"...

00:20:49.550 --> 00:20:51.980
...might have been a bit over the top.

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:57.780
Understood, Brother.

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:14.280
Hm?

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:16.650
Sara!

00:21:20.280 --> 00:21:22.280
Sara, you're using a different lipstick, aren't you?

00:21:24.180 --> 00:21:25.820
Yes, I suppose...

00:21:26.220 --> 00:21:28.980
But enough about me! Back to work!

00:21:45.120 --> 00:21:46.450
What'cha doing?

00:21:49.420 --> 00:21:51.750
I was enjoying the wind.

00:21:54.120 --> 00:21:56.150
Tiffa, look...

00:21:57.580 --> 00:22:01.250
To be honest, when I was in town, I...

00:22:01.280 --> 00:22:02.180
Garrod.

00:22:09.950 --> 00:22:14.750
Hey, isn't that lipstick? What are you doing with that?

00:22:16.920 --> 00:22:18.850
It's a secret.

00:22:22.650 --> 00:22:26.120
The boy chooses to remain a boy a while longer,

00:22:26.150 --> 00:22:29.750
and the girl is becoming a woman little by little.

00:22:30.620 --> 00:22:32.750
Garrod has put his solitary life behind him,

00:22:32.780 --> 00:22:36.380
and Tiffa has begun to reclaim her humanity.

00:22:36.980 --> 00:22:39.220
The year is AW 15.

00:22:39.320 --> 00:22:43.250
Their journey has only just begun.

00:22:45.690 --> 00:22:50.990
<b>Can I find the words to tell you</b>

00:22:45.780 --> 00:22:48.020
Can I find the words to tell you

00:22:48.050 --> 00:22:51.050
There was a boy in this snowbound town.

00:22:50.990 --> 00:22:56.370
<b>How I live between the walls of steel and stone</b>

00:22:51.120 --> 00:22:54.420
He was the emotional support of nameless people.

00:22:54.450 --> 00:22:57.450
And the mighty power that protected the town.

00:22:57.650 --> 00:23:00.880
The boy's name is Carris Nautilus.

00:22:58.040 --> 00:23:04.210
<b>How I close my eyes to find some kind of rapture</b>

00:23:00.920 --> 00:23:04.350
He is the Newtype that Jamil is searching for.

00:23:04.930 --> 00:23:10.570
<b>In a world where you can feel so all alone</b>

00:23:12.240 --> 00:23:17.550
<b>Inside I'm full of light and laughter</b>

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:21.440
<b>There's a flame that burns in me</b>

00:23:21.440 --> 00:23:22.420
<b>(I need a way)</b>

00:23:22.420 --> 00:23:26.480
<b>(I need a way) I need a way to set it free</b>

00:23:26.480 --> 00:23:31.400
<b>When you find love in your heart</b>

00:23:31.400 --> 00:23:33.530
<b>(The human touch)</b>

00:23:33.530 --> 00:23:37.590
<b>You can believe from the start</b>

00:23:37.590 --> 00:23:39.580
<b>(From the start)</b>

00:23:40.510 --> 00:23:42.710
<b>Dreams they come true</b>

00:23:42.710 --> 00:23:44.080
<b>(They come true)</b>

00:23:44.080 --> 00:23:48.420
<b>All comes to you, oh all at once</b>

00:23:48.420 --> 00:23:52.240
<b>If you believe in human touch</b>

00:23:50.050 --> 00:23:51.380
I am a Newtype.

00:23:51.380 --> 00:23:56.430
<b>Episode 10</b>

00:23:51.380 --> 00:23:56.430
<b>"I Am a Newtype"</b>

00:23:56.430 --> 00:23:58.430
<b></b>
